  "notes": "READING:\nTraditionally read こしゅう, but こしつ has become the dominant modern reading. Both are acceptable.\n\nUSAGE:\nAlmost always carries a negative nuance — the speaker views the persistence as stubborn or unreasonable. The pattern ～に{固執|こしつ}する is standard.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {意見|いけん}に{固執|こしつ}する: to insist on one's opinion\n- {前例|ぜんれい}に{固執|こしつ}する: to cling to precedent\n- {固執|こしつ}せずに: without being stubborn about\n- ～に{固執|こしつ}しすぎる: to cling too much to ~",
